# Netlify security headers for Futuro OS
# Applied on deploy (Git push). Verify live with:  curl -sI https://futurofreight.netlify.app/ | grep -i -E 'x-frame|x-content|referrer|permissions|strict-transport'
#
# NOTE: no Content-Security-Policy is set here yet. The apps rely heavily on
# inline scripts/styles (no build step), so a strict CSP needs 'unsafe-inline'
# and a full host allowlist (supabase, jsdelivr, google-fonts, nominatim,
# osrm, sam.gov, openstreetmap tiles). Add + test that against a Netlify deploy
# preview before enforcing — a wrong CSP silently breaks production.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), camera=(self), microphone=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Clickjacking protection for the operator apps (must NOT be framed anywhere).
/
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
/index.html
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
/mobile/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# The lead/carrier forms are DESIGNED to be embedded in the marketing sites,
# so instead of blocking frames we allowlist exactly those origins.
/integrations/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' https://futurosolutions.net https://futurotransport.com https://*.netlify.app
